  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/LibreDWG/libredwg/tarball/0.14",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/LibreDWG/libredwg/zipball/0.14",
  "body": "A major feature release. Encoding to r2004 dwg is now supported. \r\nEncoding to r2010, r2013 and r2018 dwg's is now experimentally possible, with CRC errors on import.\r\nMany other bugfixes. See https://www.gnu.org/software/libredwg/ and [NEWS](https://github.com/LibreDWG/libredwg/blob/0.14/NEWS)\r\n\r\nHere are the compressed sources:\r\n~~http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/libredwg/libredwg-0.14.tar.gz (21MB)~~ (error uploading)\r\n~~http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/libredwg/libredwg-0.14.tar.xz (11MB)~~\r\nhttps://github.com/LibreDWG/libredwg/releases/download/0.14/libredwg-0.14.tar.xz\r\nhttps://github.com/LibreDWG/libredwg/releases/download/0.14/libredwg-0.14.tar.gz\r\n\r\nHere are the GPG detached signatures[*]:\r\n~~http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/libredwg/libredwg-0.14.tar.gz.sig~~\r\n~~http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/libredwg/libredwg-0.14.tar.xz.sig~~\r\nhttps://github.com/LibreDWG/libredwg/releases/download/0.14/libredwg-0.14.tar.xz.sig\r\nhttps://github.com/LibreDWG/libredwg/releases/download/0.14/libredwg-0.14.tar.gz.sig\r\n\r\nUse a mirror for higher download bandwidth:\r\nhttps://www.gnu.org/order/ftp.html\r\n\r\nHere are for now all the sources and binaries:\r\nhttps://github.com/LibreDWG/libredwg/releases/tag/0.14\r\n\r\nHere are the SHA256 checksums:\r\n```\r\nb6ca1f60c7848df67cd19aa8a44684dde6108fc8852e16b58fa934982ab1e6c6  libredwg-0.14-win32.zip\r\n1ad7e15344d20b3426c3435b078d82fb84b35062815946b2cca9c5fc9810fea8  libredwg-0.14-win64.zip\r\ncb6ee0b078c6d9e0f09d66f1feac33ba6342df88ae544e9f9335fab475218351  libredwg-0.14.tar.gz\r\n62ebb73b984f865960f20ed26619ea5f8789d5e3fd088fa40a2598384da81275  libredwg-0.14.tar.xz\r\n```\r\nPlease ignore the broken Source code (tar.gz, .zip) artefacts. They cannot be deleted.\r\n\r\n[*] Use a .sig file to verify that the corresponding file (without the\r\n.sig suffix) is intact. First, be sure to download both the .sig file\r\nand the corresponding tarball. Then, run a command like this:\r\n\r\ngpg --verify libredwg-0.14.tar.gz.sig\r\n\r\nIf that command fails because you don't have the required public key,\r\nthen run this command to import it:\r\n\r\ngpg --recv-keys B4F63339E65D6414\r\n\r\nand rerun the gpg --verify command.",
